## Phase 112 closure

Phase 112 audited real mathematical workflow pressure rather than mechanically expanding the parser.

Representative workflows used:

```text
nu_prime
nu_5
sigma_11
```

The audit separated observed gaps into:

```text
parser boundary
repository lookup miss
existing-inference / specialization handoff gap
workflow orchestration gap
possible genuinely new inference / evaluator need
```

The highest-pressure minimal gap was:

```text
show-proof sigma_11
→ knows pi_18^11 = Z/16{sigma_11}

python main.py 11 7
→ previously failed to reuse the same existing specialization
```

This was classified as an orchestration gap, not as missing mathematics.

Phase 112 deliberately did not introduce a general expression parser or a general $E/H/\Delta$ evaluator.

## Phase 113 closure

Phase 113 connected the existing theorem-specific indexed $\sigma_n$ specialization to the standard `TodaGroupQuery` workflow.

The implementation is deliberately narrow:

```text
TodaGroupQuery(n, 7), n >= 10
→ existing production repository
→ existing recursive proof scope
→ existing sigma_n specialization
→ concrete group result
→ existing report / provenance pipeline
```

It does not mutate the repository and does not synthesize a result from an empty repository.

Focused Phase 113 and relevant regression tests passed, followed by the full repository regression:

```text
9081 passed in 434.58s (0:07:14)
```

